title: "JkPress: Ultra-Lightweight and High-Performance Headless Content Management System Built with Node.js"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-14
url: "https://github.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - headless-cms
  - nodejs
  - sqlite
  - seo-automation
  - geo-targeting
  - lightweight-cms
abstract: >
  JkPress is an ultra-lightweight, high-performance Headless Content Management System (CMS) 
  engineered from scratch using Node.js, Express.js, and SQLite. Designed as a streamlined 
  alternative to heavy monolithic CMS platforms, JkPress eliminates Object-Relational Mapping (ORM) 
  overhead by utilizing raw SQL execution, custom AES-256-GCM session encryption (jk-zeto), 
  built-in JSON-LD Schema Markup for AI search engine optimization, and native geo-targeting 
  capabilities for modern digital journalism.
